---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Learned ANN Index | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="An experimental recursive learned partitioner for approximate nearest-neighbor search, evaluated against IVF-PQ, HNSW, and ScaNN."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>RESEARCH PROTOTYPE · LEARNED DATA STRUCTURES · VECTOR SEARCH</p>
			<h1>Learned ANN Index</h1>
			<p>
				Can a learned recursive partition model guide embedding
				search? This prototype explores centroid-based RMI routing
				with exact or HNSW leaf search and compares quality,
				throughput, build time, and memory with IVF-PQ and optional
				HNSW/ScaNN baselines.
			</p>
			<p>
				This is a research experiment, not a claim that learned
				routing outperforms mature ANN systems. Its bundled dataset
				is synthetic; evaluate representative, authorized embeddings
				before drawing conclusions.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="algorithm">
				<h2 id="algorithm">Learned routing, measured trade-offs</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Recursive k-means routing selects candidate leaf partitions.</li>
					<li>Exact scan is the default within a partition; local HNSW is optional.</li>
					<li>Residual product quantization provides a self-contained IVF-PQ baseline.</li>
					<li>Optional adapters expose Faiss IVF-PQ, hnswlib, and ScaNN comparisons.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The benchmark reports recall@k against brute-force ground
					truth, sequential QPS, build time, and documented memory
					estimates. The Streamlit dashboard plots the recall/QPS
					frontier.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="demo">
				<h2 id="demo">Run a reproducible synthetic benchmark</h2>
				<pre><code>cd learned-ann
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev,dashboard]"
learned-ann benchmark \
  --vectors 4000 --queries 160 --dimension 32 \
  --indexes learned-rmi ivf-pq \
  --output results/ann-benchmark.json
streamlit run dashboard.py</code></pre>
				<p>
					Native baselines are optional extras; hardware, dataset,
					query batching, and index parameters affect comparisons.
					The project README documents what memory and QPS do and
					do not measure.
				</p>
				<p>
					<a href="https://github.com/buragapuravi/my_research_work/tree/main/learned-ann"
						>Read the project README</a
					>
					·
					<a href="/projects/research-chat">Explore the RAG research project</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
